Parts of the OS7 module that are written, checked, and NOT YET WIRED IN.

A file here is meant for powershell/OS7/. It is not there yet because putting it
there means naming it in four lists — OS7.psm1's foreach, hook 0060, the
os7-module .deb's required paths in build-os7-packages.sh, and OS7.psd1's
exports — and raising the function counts that check-module-parts.py holds
against CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF.md and POWERSHELL-REFERENCE.md. On 2026-10-29 another
session had four of those files open and uncommitted, and the owner chose to
build here and wire in afterwards rather than edit them underneath it.

Nothing imports this directory. check-module-parts.py does not scan it (its
pattern is powershell/OS7/OS7.*.ps1), so a file here cannot turn that check red
for anybody else. The file's own check loads it explicitly:

  OS7.Container.ps1    docs/CONTAINERS-PLAN.md CT6 and CT8, step 3.
                       installer/testing/check-container-logic.py dot-sources it
                       into the OS7 module's scope.

WIRING IT IN is a `git mv` into powershell/OS7/, its name in the four lists
(after OS7.Automation.ps1 and before OS7.Update.ps1 — the order is OS7.psm1's
to decide), its functions in OS7.psd1, and the three counts. Then this directory
goes. Delete it, do not leave it empty.
